course: dictionary
lesson: 13438
title: Strong feelings: horrified
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Horrified» is a strong word for shock. When someone is horrified, they are very shocked, upset and frightened by something terrible. Look at the words around it to check how strong the feeling is.
explain: «The villagers were horrified when they saw the flood waters rising.» A flood is terrible, and the villagers feel shock and fear. Surprised would be too weak here, because it does not show how frightened they were.
explain: Sometimes people use horrified for a small shock, as a joke. «Mum was horrified by my messy room.» Mum is not in danger. She is very shocked and disapproving. Ask yourself: is the thing really terrible, or just a bit shocking? That tells you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: «Horrified» is an adjective. It describes how a person feels.
fact: Horrify is the verb, and horrified is its past form: «The news horrified us.»
fact: «Horrified» often goes with by or at: horrified by, horrified at.
fact: «Horrified» means very shocked, upset and frightened by something terrible.
fact: In an informal way, «horrified» can mean very surprised and disapproving, as in «Mum was horrified by my messy room.»
exercise: «The sailors were horrified when the storm tore the sails.» What does horrified mean here? | Very happy and calm | Slightly bored | *Very shocked and frightened | Very hungry
exercise: «Mum was horrified by my muddy football boots on the new carpet.» What does horrified show? | Mum was lost | *Mum was very shocked and disapproving | Mum was very sleepy | Mum was ready to play football
exercise: Which word is the past form of the verb horrify? | *horrified | horrifies | horror | horrifying
test: «The children were horrified to find the injured bird on the path.» Which word is closest in meaning to horrified here? | *Shocked and upset | Sleepy | Hungry | Bored
test: «Dad was horrified at the bill for the broken window.» Why might a writer choose horrified rather than surprised? | *It shows much stronger shock and upset | It is a shorter word | It means exactly the same, so there is no reason | It means happy
exam: Which sentence uses horrified as a joke about a small shock? | «The town was horrified when the bridge collapsed.» | *«Nana was horrified that I had eaten the last biscuit.» | «The soldiers were horrified by the flood.»
